Schnitzel patch for CodeWeavers' Wine (CrossOver 26.3.0 source drop)

ntdll: per-program Wine graphics DLLs.

With D3DMetal (or DXMT) in a Pfanne, Schnitzel's engine assembly holds their DLLs in place of
Wine's own d3d DLLs. The Rockstar Games Launcher then fails to initialize: it draws with
Direct2D, Wine's d2d1 needs a Direct3D 10.1 device, and D3DMetal's dxgi.dll only has a stub
for DXGID3D10CreateDevice. CrossOver gives that launcher Wine's own DLLs (observed with lsof)
through its closed cxcompatdb.so, which calls CodeWeavers' prepend_dll_path() per program.

If the main program's Windows path ends with an entry of SCHNITZEL_WINE_GRAPHICS_PROGRAMS
(';'-separated), the folder in SCHNITZEL_WINE_GRAPHICS_DLLPATH is searched first for builtin
DLLs in that process. Schnitzel sets both and puts Wine's own copies of the replaced DLLs in
that folder (SCHNITZEL_PLAN.md, "Rockstar Games Launcher with D3DMetal 3.0").

Written for Schnitzel from scratch; licensed like Wine (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

